        "date": "2026-11-09T01:07:50Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(rest): rest machining reads the stock carried from earlier setups\n\nA rest-reading op in a setup the machined body is carried into (#317)\nnow reads what the earlier setups cut: the rest mask and the verify\nprior are the origin block, cut and carried through every boundary\ncarry::entry carries. Clip-entered setups keep their own block. The\nrest digest folds the setups crossed, each lattice turn and the origin\nstock, so a change ahead in an earlier setup stales the later op; the\nsuppressed-ahead refusal walks the same chain; a refused carry refuses\nevery reads_prior op by name (REST_CARRY_REFUSAL). Single-setup stamps\nand goldens are unchanged. rest.rs split (pilots.rs) for the 400-line law.\n\nFixes #318\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "de8b50b107d886511e4f6911622b4115ff92954b",
